title: "Elephant name calls cannot yet be separated from day effects"
abstract: "In a pre-registered test on the public data behind the 2024 elephant names study, a null that keeps each caller's day fixed could move only 11 of 469 calls. The test was valid but caught a matched names effect in 1 of 20 simulations, so these data cannot settle the dispute. Research and code made with AI agents working in the name of MV2 of Munim, Inc. Code licensed Apache-2.0; text and data CC BY 4.0 unless a file says otherwise."
